I’d give the finished café a **six-month album fed by the Daily and weekly events**, and make **one playable link the primary thing players send**. R9 already has resident requests, a forgiving streak, exact-board dares, and a strong one-seat-left replay. The next build should make those systems pay off after the house is done and carry a friend from the first message to their first move. [R9 notes](<C:/Users/Admin/Documents/Msjelly/studio/long-cat-out/qa/r9-notes.md>) · [Sol’s review](<C:/Users/Admin/Documents/Msjelly/studio/long-cat-out/qa/sol-r9-4.md>)

Everything below fits a static HTTPS build with local saves and share URLs. It requires zero accounts, backend services, or ad changes. The numbers are launch targets for the design.

## Retention · six changes

| Change | What the player gets and where it goes | What earns a pass in stills |
|---|---|---|
| **1. Give completed rooms a next move** | Replace **Floor complete!** with the next actionable build. One tap jumps to the room or shop. Example: **Library reading lamp · 2/3 stars**. From Cat Street lap three, ship **3 visible upgrades per shop across 6 shops**, priced at **2, 2, and 3 stars**. Reuse the façades and add overlays such as the Library lamp and Bakery awning. Keep an in-room resident request on its cat bubble and use the goals strip for a different goal. | On a completed ground floor, the destination, missing star, and next action are readable above **Play**. A before/after Street pair shows the lamp actually lighting up the Library. The resident request appears once. |
| **2. Give the café a permanent photo album** | Add **Album** inside Residents. Launch **6 themed pages × 4 named postcards**, enough for **24 weekly rewards**. The first card on each page can use existing resident art and a room scene. Completing a page unlocks a matching framed print the player can hang in a finished room. Each empty slot names its source and links to the event or archive. | A **3/4** page shows three distinct photos, the missing card, and exactly how to earn it. The **4/4** still shows the framed-print reward and an **Hang in café** action. A room still shows that print on the wall. |
| **3. Put a seven-day pop-up in Events** | Feature one weekly event using the Cat Show’s existing two-board flow. Earn **1 stamp from each event board** and **1 from the first Daily clear that week**. **3 stamps** unlock the postcard and **60 coins**. Ship **24 weeks of data** with solver-checked layouts and a featured shop or resident. When a week ends, its coin reward closes and the postcard moves to an archive with **1 catch-up postcard per week**. The four-week Season keeps its visitor track. | Events opens on a card that reads **Library Reading Week · 2/3 · 1d 11h left** and shows the postcard and the one remaining action. A rollover still shows the new event and the old postcard available in the archive. |
| **4. Make Daily clears count toward something lasting** | Keep the existing **one missed-day shield per week** and daily chest payouts. Add a permanent Daily record with rewards at **7, 14, 30, 60, and 90 total clears**. At **7 and 14**, grant **1 Hint** and **1 Undo**, respectively. At **30, 60, and 90**, unlock a portrait frame, a café pennant, and a wall clock. Put the next milestone on the Daily sheet and in the Daily win summary. Credit each date once. | A Day 29 win shows **29/30 clears** beside a silhouette of the frame. A missed-day pair shows the shield consumed and the total preserved. At Day 30, the unlocked frame appears on the resident portrait. |
| **5. Make today’s request belong to a specific cat** | Use Tasks to show **2 rotating resident jobs each day** and pay for the **first one completed**. Seed a **14-day rotation** from existing win, cat, carrier, and tidy-clear hooks. Examples: **Help Dewey shelve 6 carriers** or **Clear a board with at most 2 cushions for Bun**. Pay **30 coins + 1 heart** to the featured cat. After claim, the same slot shows tomorrow’s cat and reset time. | The hub shows a named cat, one measurable goal, and the reward together. Capture **4/6**, **Claim**, and **Tomorrow · Bun**. At 375×667, the task fits in the existing two-tile strip with **Play** fully visible. |
| **6. Let real friend results give players a reason to reopen** | Add **Friend Results** to Events and put **Rematch** next to the most recent imported result. Opening a reply link imports a replay-checked result on that browser. Keep the **latest 12 results**, deduplicated by result ID. A card might read **Ana matched your ×3 · Level 13 · 5 cushions**. One tap reopens that exact board. This gives the café real social proof from the links players receive. | A fresh save reads **Open a friend’s result link to start**. After importing a reply, the card shows both scores, the board, and **Rematch**. Reopening the same reply leaves one entry. |

## Virality · six changes

| Change | What the player gets and where it goes | What earns a pass in stills |
|---|---|---|
| **1. Send one playable dare from the win card** | **Dare a friend** opens the native share sheet in **1 game tap**, with **1 HTTPS URL** ready before clip encoding. Offer **Copy dare link** where native sharing is unavailable and a selectable URL if copying fails. Generate **8 static Open Graph cards** at build time for chain, clean sweep, Daily, and reply, in EN and TR. The opened page renders the exact score and replay from the URL payload. | Capture the win card while encoding, the actual received chat bubble, and the opened dare. The button is ready on the win card, one message contains the playable link, and that message opens the intended board. [Web Share API](https://www.w3.org/TR/web-share/) · [Open Graph protocol](https://ogp.me/) |
| **2. Put the exact dare inside every clip** | Keep the **720×1280** vertical replay and the one-seat-left opener. Burn a short, typeable challenge URL into a safe strip for the **entire 6–9 second clip**. Add a QR to the same exact board, seat count, and goal on the **final 3 seconds** and on the PNG fallback. A compact versioned token carries the challenge without a URL-shortening service. | The opening, peak, end card, and fallback PNG all carry the URL. At **360 px wide**, the URL is readable and the QR scans from a chat-transcoded copy. The decoded board, seats, and goal agree with the caption. Share targets can discard accompanying fields, which is why the link belongs in the image itself. [Web Share API share-target behavior](https://www.w3.org/TR/web-share/#share-targets) |
| **3. Land on the challenge in one tap** | Open directly on **Ana dares you · Beat ×3 · Level 13 · 5 cushions**, with a muted replay preview when the link carries one. **Play dare** starts the exact board in **1 tap**. On a fresh browser, keep the current carrier and cushion highlights through the first move. Pin the board generator revision in the token and continue decoding existing `?c=` links. | Capture the received link opening and the first playable frame. The goal, level, and seat count agree across both. The carrier and cushion are legible on the first board, and the **Play dare** button fits on the landing at 375×667 in EN and TR. |
| **4. Give every clear a reply worth sending** | Show both scores on the result sheet with **Send result** as the main action. Example: **Ana ×3 · You ×4**. A tie gets **I matched it**, and a clear below target gets **Send result** and **Try again**. The reply link carries the original challenge ID, the result, and a bounded move log. The browser replays the log before putting the score in Friend Results. | Capture beat, tie, and below-target results. Each shows the two scores and an obvious reply action. Then open the reply on the original sender’s browser and capture the same result with **Rematch**. |
| **5. Let a dare travel beyond the original pair** | After a match or beat, offer **Pass it on** alongside **Send result**. Keep the exact board and seat count, set the next target from the player’s result, and carry the **latest 3 replay-checked runs**. Use the existing board-ceiling check to turn a max-chain result into **Match ×5**. The next friend can answer or pass it on again. | A third-person landing shows **Ana ×3 → Deniz ×4 → Your turn**, with one clear target. A ceiling case shows **Match ×5** on both landing and board. The thread remains readable in the Turkish short-phone capture. |
| **6. Ask for a share at the moment that tells a story** | Feature **Dare a friend** on **three** win moments: a **×3+ bench chain**, a **zero-park clear on a board with 10+ cats**, and a **first clear of today’s Daily**. Give each its own headline and use the actual peak frame in the win card. Show the explanatory nudge **once per browser**, on the first qualifying win. Keep ordinary wins focused on **Next** and friend wins focused on the reply. | Capture a one-seat-left ×3, a zero-park clear, a Daily first clear, and an ordinary win. Each featured card makes the feat legible in one glance. The ordinary win keeps **Next** visually dominant, and the featured cards keep both buttons visible at 375×667. |

## Build order and the 8+ bar

1. **First playable slice:** ship the completed-room card, the first album page and event, and the single-link dare through landing and reply. That tests both loops end to end with existing art.
2. **Then build out the calendar and relay:** load all 24 weeks, add the Daily milestones and rotating requests, ship the Street overlays, and finish the clip URL, QR, and pass-along flow.
3. **Score the result on visible evidence and actual handoffs.** For retention, capture a completed-house save on an ordinary day, after a claim, after a missed day, at weekly rollover, and at weeks 4, 12, and 24. Each state needs a visible next action, a specific payoff, and a reason to return. For virality, run sender → received message → first move → reply on **iPhone/iMessage, iPhone/WhatsApp, and Android/WhatsApp**. Test a clipboard refusal and a received file with its caption removed. Require every supported route to reach the exact dare from one message or from the link burned into the file.

Capture the critical states in **EN and TR at 375×667**. Stills can earn the 8+ **design** score for clarity and progression. Physical-phone tests establish delivery, and the existing local counters can support playtests. Population retention and viral lift remain unmeasured with this setup.
